---
import LuxeLayout from '../layouts/LuxeLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '9 August 2026';
---

<LuxeLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — LUXEhome"
  description="How LUXEhome collects, uses, shares and protects information submitted through our website and site inspection form, and how to request deletion."
>
  <section class="policy-hero">
    <p class="lx-eyebrow">Legal · Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy.</h1>
    <p class="policy-intro">This policy explains what information LUXEhome collects through luxehome.lk, why we use it, who may process it and how you can ask us to access, correct or delete it.</p>
    <p class="policy-date">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
  </section>

  <div class="policy-layout">
    <article class="policy-document">
      <section id="who-we-are">
        <p class="policy-number">01</p>
        <div>
          <h2>Who we are</h2>
          <p>LUXEhome is a Sri Lankan bathroom design and construction business and a sister brand of TILERSHUB. For the information described in this policy, LUXEhome decides why and how it is used.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="information-we-collect">
        <p class="policy-number">02</p>
        <div>
          <h2>Information we collect</h2>
          <p>When you submit the site inspection form, we collect your name, phone or WhatsApp number, email address if you provide it, and property location. We also collect the project details you enter, such as the project type, preferred design, approximate bathroom size, preferred appointment date and time, and notes.</p>
          <p>If you continue the conversation on WhatsApp or email, we may receive the messages, photographs, videos, measurements and other project information you choose to send.</p>
          <p>Our website and its service providers may also process technical and usage information such as your IP address, browser or device information, referring page, pages viewed and interactions with the site. Google Analytics and Meta technologies are used to measure site visits, advertising and form conversions.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="how-we-use-information">
        <p class="policy-number">03</p>
        <div>
          <h2>How we use your information</h2>
          <p>We use this information to respond to your request, confirm the service area and appointment, arrange and carry out the site inspection, understand your bathroom requirements, prepare the design and proposal, communicate decisions and documents, and maintain records if the project proceeds.</p>
          <p>We also use limited information to operate and secure the website, understand which pages and advertisements are useful, improve our services, prevent misuse, meet legal or accounting duties, and establish or respond to contractual or legal claims.</p>
          <p>We process project-request information to take steps you ask us to take before a contract and, if appointed, to perform the contract. We may also process information where necessary for our legitimate business interests, legal obligations or your consent, as applicable.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="communications">
        <p class="policy-number">04</p>
        <div>
          <h2>WhatsApp and email communication</h2>
          <p>After you submit a request, LUXEhome may contact you by WhatsApp and by email, when an email address is provided, about the inspection, payment instructions, design, proposal, quotation, construction or aftercare. WhatsApp communications are also subject to WhatsApp and Meta’s own privacy terms.</p>
          <p>We do not use an inspection request as permission for unrelated mass marketing. Where a promotional message requires your consent, we will ask for it, identify LUXEhome and provide a way to opt out.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing">
        <p class="policy-number">05</p>
        <div>
          <h2>Who may receive or process it</h2>
          <p>We share personal information only where reasonably necessary with authorised LUXEhome team members and project specialists, website hosting and security providers, database and business-system providers, email providers, and communication, analytics and advertising services including WhatsApp and Meta, Google Analytics, Supabase and Cloudflare.</p>
          <p>Some providers operate internationally, so information may be processed outside Sri Lanka under their applicable safeguards and terms. We may also disclose information to professional advisers, regulators, courts or public authorities where required by law or necessary to protect legal rights. We do not sell your personal information.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="retention-security">
        <p class="policy-number">06</p>
        <div>
          <h2>Retention and security</h2>
          <p>We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the inquiry or project, client support, operational records, security, accounting and tax requirements, and the establishment or defence of legal claims. The exact period depends on whether you proceed with a project and any legal record-keeping duty. When information is no longer needed, we delete or anonymise it where reasonably possible.</p>
          <p>We use reasonable access controls and technical and organisational safeguards intended to protect information against unauthorised access, loss or misuse. No online or electronic system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="your-rights">
        <p class="policy-number">07</p>
        <div>
          <h2>Access, correction and deletion</h2>
          <p>You may write to us to ask whether we hold your personal information, request access or correction, withdraw consent where processing is based on consent, object to certain further processing, or request deletion where the applicable law gives you that right.</p>
          <p>To request deletion, email <a href="mailto:luxehome@gmail.com">luxehome@gmail.com</a> or send a WhatsApp message to <a href="https://wa.me/94774503744" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">+94 77 450 3744</a>. Include the name, phone number or email address used in your request and clearly state that you want your data deleted. We may ask for enough information to verify your identity.</p>
          <p>We will tell you in writing within 21 working days whether the request has been granted. We may retain information where the law requires or permits it, including records needed for accounting, an active contract, safety, fraud prevention or a legal claim; if so, we will explain the reason unless the law prevents us from doing so.</p>
          <p>You may also have the right to complain to the <a href="https://www.dpa.gov.lk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data Protection Authority of Sri Lanka</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <p class="policy-number">08</p>
        <div>
          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy when our services, systems or legal obligations change. The latest version will remain on this page with its updated date.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>

    <aside class="policy-contact" aria-label="LUXEhome privacy contact details">
      <p class="lx-eyebrow">Privacy contact</p>
      <h2>LUXEhome</h2>
      <p>Sri Lanka</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Email</dt><dd><a href="mailto:luxehome@gmail.com">luxehome@gmail.com</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>WhatsApp / phone</dt><dd><a href="https://wa.me/94774503744" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">+94 77 450 3744</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Website</dt><dd><a href="https://luxehome.lk">luxehome.lk</a></dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="policy-contact-note">For a privacy request, include the contact details you used so we can locate the correct record.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</LuxeLayout>

<style>
  .policy-hero,
  .policy-layout { width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 34px)); margin-inline: auto; }
  .policy-hero { padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem) 0 clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(43, 50, 42, .12); }
  .policy-hero h1 { margin: .65rem 0 1.1rem; max-width: 900px; font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 8vw, 5.6rem); }
  .policy-intro { max-width: 760px; font: 500 clamp(1.16rem, 2.4vw, 1.35rem)/1.5 var(--lx-serif); }
  .policy-date { margin-top: 1.15rem; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 58%, transparent); font-size: .82rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .policy-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px; align-items: start; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) 0 5rem; }
  .policy-document { min-width: 0; }
  .policy-document section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 44px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1rem; padding: 0 0 2.4rem; margin-bottom: 2.4rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(43, 50, 42, .1); scroll-margin-top: 100px; }
  .policy-document section:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .policy-number { color: var(--gold); font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; }
  .policy-document h2,
  .policy-contact h2 { margin: -.22rem 0 .8rem; font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3vw, 2.35rem); }
  .policy-document p { color: #586057; }
  .policy-document p + p { margin-top: .9rem; }
  .policy-document a,
  .policy-contact a { color: var(--sage-deep); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .policy-contact { position: sticky; top: 100px; padding: 26px; border: 1px solid rgba(43, 50, 42, .12); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(43, 50, 42, .06); }
  .policy-contact > p:not(.lx-eyebrow) { color: #586057; }
  .policy-contact dl { margin: 1.4rem 0; }
  .policy-contact dl div { padding: .8rem 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(43, 50, 42, .1); }
  .policy-contact dt { margin-bottom: .2rem; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 58%, transparent); font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .policy-contact dd { margin: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .policy-contact-note { font-size: .84rem; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .policy-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .policy-contact { position: static; grid-row: 1; }
    .policy-document section { grid-template-columns: 34px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .65rem; }
  }
</style>
